accel/tcg: a retired-guest-instruction budget with a callback

Adds an optional budget, independent of icount: count retired guest
instructions with icount's own decrementer, and when a quantum expires at a TB
boundary, refill it and call a hook. The hook runs on the vCPU thread with
consistent CPU state and no BQL held.

It exists to couple a second emulated chip to guest progress rather than to
host time: both chips then advance in a fixed ratio, the way two crystals fix
them in hardware, and a run is reproducible. TBs are instrumented only when
icount or this budget asks for it, and CF_NOIRQ blocks — which have no exit
label to leave through — are left alone.

